<section class="card searchable" id="quick"><h2><span class="n">01</span> Quick Start: पहली बार ऐप कैसे इस्तेमाल करें</h2>
<p>Diploma Engineers में अपनी जरूरत के अनुसार सही section खोलें। कुछ resources सीधे खुल सकते हैं, जबकि paid course या profile-based features के लिए login आवश्यक हो सकता है।</p>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open the app or website</strong><span>Use the official Diploma Engineers app/site link provided by the team. If a page does not load, check your internet and reload once.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Choose your study section</strong><span>Notes, Books & Notes, Syllabus, PYQ, Test Series, Results, Admit Card and JEECUP may appear in the app menu or home page.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Select branch and semester</strong><span>When asked, select the correct engineering branch and semester. Some early semesters may use common subjects, while later semesters can be branch-specific.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open the resource and verify it</strong><span>Check the subject, semester and title before reading or downloading a PDF. Use the back button inside the page to return to the previous list.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Sign in only when needed</strong><span>Use your own account for profile, purchases, course access or saved progress. Never share your password or OTP.</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="note ok"><b>Best habit:</b> Select the correct branch + semester first, then select subject/topic. It reduces the chance of opening the wrong study material.</div>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="account"><h2><span class="n">02</span> Account, login and profile</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="tile"><h3><i class="fa-solid fa-right-to-bracket"></i> Login</h3><p>Use the login method shown in your app. Enter the registered details carefully and wait for the success response.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3><i class="fa-solid fa-id-card"></i> Profile</h3><p>Where profile editing is available, update your name, branch, semester, college and profile photo accurately.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3><i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i> Account security</h3><p>Keep OTPs and passwords private. Log out on shared devices and avoid saving credentials on public computers.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3><i class="fa-solid fa-rotate"></i> Session problems</h3><p>If your profile or purchased content does not appear, check that you are logged into the same account used for the purchase.</p></div>
</div>
<h3>Profile update steps</h3><ol><li>Open Profile or Account.</li><li>Choose Edit Profile if available.</li><li>Update only the fields you want to change.</li><li>Tap Save and wait for confirmation.</li><li>Reopen the profile to check that the changes persisted.</li></ol>
<div class="note warn">If you cannot log in, do not repeatedly create new accounts. Check the login method and use the app's official support/contact option.</div>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="notes"><h2><span class="n">03</span> Notes, books and PDF resources</h2>
<p>Use Notes or Books & Notes to find subject-wise study material, notes, e-books and other PDF resources that are available in the app.</p>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open Notes / Books & Notes</strong><span>Choose the resource section from Home or navigation.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Select branch and semester</strong><span>For common subjects, choose the common option if shown. Otherwise choose your branch and the semester you are studying.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Choose subject, book or PDF</strong><span>Read the title and description to confirm the resource matches your course.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open, read or download</strong><span>Use the PDF viewer or download control if provided. Some links may open in a separate browser tab.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Return to the list</strong><span>Use the page's Back button or the app navigation. If a PDF is blank, refresh it or open its link in your browser.</span></div></div>
</div>
<h3>When a PDF will not open</h3><ul><li>Check internet connectivity and try again.</li><li>Confirm the PDF is not still loading; wait a few seconds.</li><li>Try opening the link in a modern browser or PDF reader.</li><li>If the link says access denied or file not found, report the resource title to support.</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="syllabus"><h2><span class="n">04</span> Syllabus, PYQ and JEECUP resources</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="tile"><h3>Syllabus</h3><p>Open Syllabus, select branch and semester, then open the subject/unit information. Use it to plan which units and topics to study.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3>PYQ (Previous Year Questions)</h3><p>Open PYQ, choose branch, semester and subject where available, then browse the matching paper. Check the year and subject before preparing from it.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3>JEECUP</h3><p>Open the JEECUP section for the entrance-exam information, resources or practice features published there. Read the instructions attached to each resource.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3>Search and filters</h3><p>If search, branch or semester filters are shown, use them to narrow the list. Clear the filter if the resource seems to be missing.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="note">Always verify exam dates, eligibility and official notices against the relevant official authority. Study resources are for preparation and may not replace an official notice.</div>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="tests"><h2><span class="n">05</span> Test Series: start a test and check your result</h2>
<p>Test Series can help you practise MCQs and review your performance when a published test is available. Available filters and test settings depend on the test.</p>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open Test Series</strong><span>Choose the Test Series feature from Home or the navigation menu.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Filter the test list</strong><span>Select branch, semester, subject or topic if filters are available. Read the title, question count and duration.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Read instructions before starting</strong><span>Check the language, time limit, marks, negative marking and navigation rules shown on the instruction screen.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Agree and begin</strong><span>If the test requires an “I Agree” confirmation, read the instructions and select it to proceed.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Answer and submit</strong><span>Choose an option for each question. Review unanswered questions if time permits, then use Submit/Finish and confirm if prompted.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Review result and analysis</strong><span>Check score, correct/incorrect answers and any available analysis/history. If a result card can be shared, review it before sharing.</span></div></div>
</div>
<h3>Test-taking tips</h3><ul><li>Use a stable internet connection and avoid refreshing during an active test unless instructed.</li><li>Do not close the app until the submission/result screen appears.</li><li>If the test freezes, note the test title and time, then contact support; do not assume the attempt was saved.</li><li>Check the correct answer key and explanations after submission where available.</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="courses"><h2><span class="n">06</span> Paid courses, purchase and course access</h2>
<p>Some course content may be paid or restricted. The exact payment method, price and access rules are shown in the app at the time of purchase.</p>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open Courses / Unlock Courses</strong><span>Browse the available courses and read the title, branch, included semesters, description and fee.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Confirm course details before paying</strong><span>Check the course is for your branch/semester and review what content is included. Do not rely only on the thumbnail or course name.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Follow the displayed payment instructions</strong><span>If a QR/UPI payment flow is shown, pay only to the displayed verified destination and for the displayed amount.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Submit payment reference if requested</strong><span>Enter the correct transaction reference/UTR and other required details. Do not submit a guessed or reused reference.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Wait for verification</strong><span>Some purchases require manual approval. Keep the transaction confirmation until access is granted or support resolves the request.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open your unlocked course</strong><span>After approval, refresh the app or sign in again if necessary. Open the course and choose the semester, subject, folder, video or PDF.</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="note warn"><b>Payment safety:</b> Never share your UPI PIN, banking password, OTP or card PIN. A payment screenshot alone is not a guarantee of course access; use the official verification workflow.</div>
<h3>Purchased course is still locked</h3><ol><li>Check that you are signed into the same account used to submit the purchase request.</li><li>Check the request status, if a status page is provided.</li><li>Refresh the course list or reopen the app.</li><li>If it remains locked, contact support with the course title, transaction date and request reference. Hide sensitive payment information.</li></ol>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="coupons"><h2><span class="n">07</span> Coupon codes and discounts</h2>
<p>If a coupon code is available, read the offer terms and apply the code in the designated coupon field before completing the purchase.</p>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><div><strong>Find the coupon code</strong><span>Use a code supplied by the official Diploma Engineers channel, Founder or authorized admin.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Copy the code exactly</strong><span>Avoid extra spaces, punctuation or changing letters/numbers.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Apply the coupon where requested</strong><span>Enter it in the checkout/coupon field and press Apply or Validate if shown.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Check the final price</strong><span>Confirm that the discount is actually reflected before paying. If the price does not change, do not assume the coupon worked.</span></div></div>
</div>
<h3>Coupon not working?</h3><ul><li>Check spelling and any displayed expiry or eligibility conditions.</li><li>Confirm that the code applies to the course you selected.</li><li>Try copying it again without spaces.</li><li>If the app shows invalid/expired, contact the issuer rather than repeatedly submitting payment.</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="results"><h2><span class="n">08</span> Results, admit cards and exam updates</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div class="tile"><h3>Results</h3><p>Open Result, enter the details requested by the page, verify them carefully and follow the displayed instructions to view or save the result.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3>Admit Card</h3><p>Open Admit Card and choose the relevant exam/session if shown. Enter only the required information and check name, roll number, exam centre and dates on the downloaded document.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3>Official information</h3><p>Use links to official portals when provided. If a portal is temporarily unavailable, try again later rather than submitting details to an unofficial website.</p></div>
<div class="tile"><h3>Save a copy</h3><p>Download or print the document when the official page allows it. Keep personal exam documents private.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="note warn">If the page requests a roll number, registration number or other personal detail, enter it only on the correct trusted page. Check the URL before submitting.</div>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="community"><h2><span class="n">09</span> Feedback, contact and community links</h2>
<p>Use the app's Feedback or Contact section to report an issue, suggest a feature or share a correction. Official WhatsApp/Telegram links, when shown inside the app, can be used for announcements and community updates.</p>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><div><strong>Open Feedback / Contact</strong><span>Enter the details requested by the form and describe your issue clearly.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Explain the issue in one message</strong><span>Include the page, action, error and what you expected. Avoid sending repeated messages for the same issue.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Use official community links</strong><span>Open the channel link from the app or verified official page. Be cautious of people impersonating admins or offering unofficial paid access.</span></div></div>
<div class="step"><div><strong>Wait for a response</strong><span>Some issues require technical review. Keep the error text and reference details until the issue is resolved.</span></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="safety"><h2><span class="n">10</span> Safety, privacy and responsible use</h2>
<ul><li>Never share OTPs, passwords, UPI PINs or banking credentials with anyone claiming to be support.</li><li>Verify the course name, fee, payment destination and discount before confirming payment.</li><li>Do not post private profile details, transaction references or admit cards in public groups.</li><li>Use study materials for learning and respect the creator's copyright and usage conditions.</li><li>Check official exam notices for deadlines, eligibility, fees and result dates.</li><li>Do not install APKs or open payment links sent by unknown accounts; use official app/site links.</li><li>Report broken links, incorrect answers or suspicious payment requests through the official contact route.</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="problems"><h2><span class="n">11</span> Troubleshooting: common problems and fixes</h2>
<div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Try this first</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>App/page does not open</td><td>Check internet, reload once, try a current browser and open the official URL again.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Login fails</td><td>Check the login details and account. Use the official recovery/support method if available.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Notes or books do not appear</td><td>Check branch/semester/subject filters, clear search and refresh the list.</td></tr>
<tr><td>PDF is blank or not loading</td><td>Wait for loading, reopen the link in a browser/PDF reader and check whether the file is still available.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Test result not shown</td><td>Wait for submission to finish, check test history if available and avoid starting another attempt until status is clear.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Course is locked after payment</td><td>Check the same account, request status and approval workflow; then contact support with the course/request reference.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Coupon not accepted</td><td>Copy the code again, check terms/expiry and verify the discount is reflected before payment.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Back button does not work</td><td>Use the in-page Back control, wait for the screen to load, and avoid browser Back if it exits the workflow. Reload only after preserving unsaved details.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Profile changes disappear</td><td>Save and wait for confirmation, reopen the profile and check that the same account is signed in.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Something still does not work</td><td>Capture the exact error and page name; report device/browser, approximate time and steps to reproduce. Hide private information in screenshots.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h3>How to report a useful bug</h3><ol><li>What page were you on?</li><li>Which button did you tap?</li><li>What did you expect to happen?</li><li>What actually happened, including exact error text?</li><li>Does the issue continue after refresh or signing in again?</li></ol>
</section>
<section class="card searchable" id="faq"><h2><span class="n">12</span> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq" id="faqItems">
<details><summary>How do I find notes for my semester?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Open Notes/Books & Notes, select your branch and semester, then choose the subject or resource.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>Why can I not see my branch or semester?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Check whether you opened the right section, clear filters and refresh. If the option is genuinely missing, contact support with your branch and semester details.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>Are all books and courses free?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Not necessarily. Check the displayed price and access terms on each resource/course before proceeding.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>How do I know whether my course payment was accepted?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Check the request status in the app if available and wait for the stated verification process. Keep your transaction confirmation.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>Can I use a coupon after paying?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Do not assume a coupon can be applied after payment. Apply it at the designated checkout stage and verify the final amount before paying.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>Can I leave a test and come back later?</summary><div class="answer"><p>That depends on the test's rules and whether progress is saved. Read the instructions before starting and do not close the test unless the interface explains how attempts are handled.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>My test score looks wrong. What should I do?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Check the answer review/analysis if available. Report the test title, question number and expected issue; do not share a private student account publicly.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>Why does a PDF link say access denied?</summary><div class="answer"><p>The file may not be publicly accessible or may have been removed. Report the resource title and link destination to the support team.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>How do I contact the team?</summary><div class="answer"><p>Use the app's Feedback or Contact section, or use the verified official community links shown in the app.</p></div></details>
